[ambates@orion.arc.nasa.gov (Andrew M Bates) writes:]
[] What is the relation between different colored unicorns and your alignment?
[] Should you try to kill unicorns of other alignments?  And what does it mean
[] on you intrinsics when it says "Good luck does not time out for you" or
[] the same for bad luck?  I've been throwing gems at unicorns, and I have
[] extra luck.

unicorns come in three colors, black, gray and white.  alignment comes
in three flavors, chaotic, neutral and lawful.  each unicorn of a
certain color belongs to the same alignment.  unicorns of your alignment
won't (normally) attack you.  look at which ones attack you (using the
"/" command, if possible).  as a rule (made to be broken) you should
attack anything that attacks you and avoid attacking anything which
avoids attacking you.

identifying your stones could be very beneficial to you.

when your intrinsics say that "Good luck does not time out for you", etc.
it means that for some reason your luck is being influenced.  normally,
luck can increase or decrease significantly in response to some action
of yours. over time this change in luck gradually erodes back to zero.
in your case, your luck is frozen, it does not erode but it will still
change in response to actions of yours.  if you have bad luck it will
stay bad luck until you cause it change.  same for good luck.  that you
have extra luck means ... well, you've acquired extra luck somehow.

that good and bad luck don't time out for you doesn't seem like a
blessing or a curse does it?

oh yeah, about stoning those unicorns, it's hard to interpret what
your intentions are when you stone unicorns not of your alignment.

